{"tool_name":"multimap_multi-omics","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"multimap_multi-omics","home":"http://github.com/Teichlab/MultiMAP","license":"MIT","summary":"Dimensionality reduction and integration of multimodal data.","addition_date":"2022-05-19T22:36:26.502135Z","last_update_date":"2022-05-19T22:36:26.504647Z","tool_type":["Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:multimap_multi-omics","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"m.efremova@qmul.ac.uk","name":"Mirjana Efremova","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8107-9974","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"mikasarkinjain@gmail.com","name":"Mika Sarkin Jain","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"st9@sanger.ac.uk","name":"Sarah A. Teichmann","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Dimensionality reduction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3935"},{"term":"Essential dynamics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3891"},{"term":"Gene expression profiling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0314"}]}],"name":"MultiMAP","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/S13059-021-02565-Y","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021, The Author(s).Multimodal data is rapidly growing in many fields of science and engineering, including single-cell biology. We introduce MultiMAP, a novel algorithm for dimensionality reduction and integration. MultiMAP can integrate any number of datasets, leverages features not present in all datasets, is not restricted to a linear mapping, allows the user to specify the influence of each dataset, and is extremely scalable to large datasets. We apply MultiMAP to single-cell transcriptomics, chromatin accessibility, methylation, and spatial data and show that it outperforms current approaches. On a new thymus dataset, we use MultiMAP to integrate cells along a temporal trajectory. This enables quantitative comparison of transcription factor expression and binding site accessibility over the course of T cell differentiation, revealing patterns of expression versus binding site opening kinetics.","authors":[{"name":"Botting R.A."},{"name":"Chen X."},{"name":"Conde C.D."},{"name":"Efremova M."},{"name":"Haniffa M."},{"name":"Jain M.S."},{"name":"Knights A."},{"name":"Lamacraft A."},{"name":"Mamanova L."},{"name":"Park J."},{"name":"Polanski K."},{"name":"Stephenson E."},{"name":"Teichmann S.A."}],"date":"2021-12-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Genome Biology","title":"MultiMAP: dimensionality reduction and integration of multimodal data"},"pmcid":"PMC8686224","pmid":"34930412"}],"topic":[{"term":"Cell biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2229"},{"term":"Chromosome conformation capture","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3940"},{"term":"RNA-Seq","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3170"},{"term":"Transcription factors and regulatory sites","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0749"},{"term":"Transcriptomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3308"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"MultiMAP","home":"https://bio.tools/multimap_multi-omics","license":"MIT","summary":"Dimensionality reduction and integration of multimodal data.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:multimap_multi-omics/lib/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":53,"citations":[{"count":8,"year":"2023"},{"count":9,"year":"2022"},{"count":11,"year":"2024"},{"count":11,"year":"2026"},{